# Generated by scripts/docs/*.py — never hand-merged, always regenerated.
#
# The `regen-docs` driver takes the incoming side wholesale and records that a
# regeneration is owed; run `dev docs index` after the merge. The driver
# DEFINITION lives in .git/config, which is not version controlled — install it with
# `python scripts/git/install_merge_drivers.py`, and `dev check merge-drivers`
# asserts it is there. This named a `dev setup` that docs/DEVELOPMENT.md explains
# in bold cannot exist: the CLI needs the virtualenv that setup would create. Without it git
# falls back to a three-way text merge of these files, which is never a correct
# resolution: conflict markers inside a generated JSON, hand-resolved, are how a
# branch's doc edits get silently reverted.
docs/todo_index.json            merge=regen-docs
docs/TODO/README.md             merge=regen-docs
docs/implementation_index.json  merge=regen-docs
docs/implementations/README.md  merge=regen-docs

# Normalize line endings so a Windows checkout does not rewrite every file.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
